# Everything here is EXCLUDED from the Docker build context — the tarball the
# daemon receives before a single instruction runs. Without this file that
# tarball is about 7GB, and `docker build` spends minutes uploading data the
# image then throws away.

# 6.1GB, and a Windows virtualenv is useless in a Linux image regardless: the
# Dockerfile installs Linux wheels from requirements.txt.
.venv/
venv/
env/

# chroma_db/ is deliberately NOT ignored.
#
# On Cloud Run the index has to ship inside the image, because the platform
# gives a container no persistent disk — see the long note on CHROMA_DIR in the
# Dockerfile. That makes the build context ~553MB rather than 96KB and the
# push correspondingly slow, which is the price of scale-to-zero hosting.
#
# If you move to a host WITH a disk (Fly, a VM), uncomment the line below and
# point CHROMA_DIR at the mount instead. The Dockerfile note explains what
# changes.
#
# chroma_db/

# 71MB of concatenated Yelp reviews, an input to the one-time seed scripts.
tagged_reviews.txt
data/
*.parquet
*.csv
*.json

# Secrets never belong in an image layer. Config comes from the environment.
.env
.env.*

# Notebooks, git history and IDE state are not needed to serve requests.
*.ipynb
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.git/
.gitignore
.idea/
.vscode/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# A stray package.json pulled these in; nothing Python uses them.
node_modules/
package-lock.json
